As of Tuesday morning (Sept. 22), Swift&#8217;s website automatically redirects to the following domain: https://store.taylorswift.com/password. It displays a red curtain background with clock numbers steadily ticking down, as well as a note confirming that the countdown &#8220;ends Sep 22 at 2pm ET.&#8221;

Billboard has reached out to Swift&#8217;s rep for comment.

Fans will have to wait until then to find out what the 14-time Grammy winner is up to. For now, all they have to go on is the mysterious to Swift&#8217;s Instagram bio and The Life of a Showgirl lyrics on Apple Music, where all the letter O&#8217;s are replaced with zeros.

“And, baby, that’s sh0w business f0r y0u,” her bio now reads.

Swift also dropped Easter eggs in her recent Law & Order: SVU parody shown at the 2026 Emmys. Portraying a rookie detective alongside star Mariska Hargitay, the singer stared directly into the camera and hinted : “Saccharide. Ares. From the Vineyard. North or South.”

Naturally, fans are freaking out. Some theorize that the pending announcement must have something to do with Swift&#8217;s 2025 12-week Billboard 200 -topping album, noting the aesthetic of the countdown. &#8220;okay so def showgirl related,&#8221; one Swiftie wrote on X, resharing a screengrab of Swift&#8217;s website. &#8220;Could be: tour, music video, deluxe album.&#8221;

Others have put together that the third letters of each of the words she pointedly said on the SVU skit can be rearranged to spell the word &#8220;Encore.&#8221;

There are also a number of fans who think the announcement has something to do with the long awaited Taylor Swift (Taylor&#8217;s Version) re-record of Swift&#8217;s 2006 debut album. &#8220;My gut says 000 = 0:00 — a clock reset,&#8221; one person wrote . &#8220;We’re going back to the beginning. With Debut’s 20th anniversary next month + Taylor saying the remaining re-records would now be a &#8216;celebration,&#8217; I think we’re finally getting that anticipated ‘20th Anniversary Deluxe’ with vault tracks.&#8221;
